<mujoco model="contact_site_frame_test">
  <!-- contact_minimal.xml plus a SECOND reference site on the same body,
       carrying a non-identity rotation relative to it.

       WHY A SECOND SITE RATHER THAN ROTATING THE FIRST. Both frames have to be
       reachable from ONE scene so the two reference_frame modes can be compared
       on bit-identical physics. Rotating tip_a_ft_site instead would change what
       "body" mode reports as well, and then a difference between the two runs
       would prove nothing about which rotation was applied.

       Both sites sit at pos="0 0 0", so the torque shift to the site origin is
       identical for the two modes and the ONLY thing that can differ is the
       rotation. That isolation is the point: a test where position and rotation
       both move cannot say which one a regression broke.

       WHY THIS PARTICULAR QUAT. (w,x,y,z) = (0.5,-0.5,-0.5,0.5) is the rotation
       R = [[0,0,-1],[1,0,0],[0,-1,0]], which maps every body axis onto a
       DIFFERENT site axis and flips two signs:
           v_site = R^T v_body = ( v_body.y, -v_body.z, -v_body.x )
       So a component transposition, a dropped transpose (R instead of R^T), and
       a silent fallback to the identity each produce a different answer.
       A symmetric rotation — 180 deg about an axis, say — would let a
       transposition pass. It is also the exact rotation ur5e_p1b's thumb
       bracket carries relative to its tip link, which is the case that made
       this option necessary. -->
  <compiler angle="radian"/>
  <option timestep="0.002" gravity="0 0 -9.81"/>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="arm_base" pos="0 0 0.50">
      <joint name="j1" type="hinge" axis="0 1 0" range="-3.14 3.14" damping="0.5"/>
      <inertial pos="0 0 -0.20" mass="0.5" diaginertia="0.005 0.005 0.005"/>
      <geom type="capsule" fromto="0 0 0 0 0 -0.40" size="0.01"
            rgba="0.6 0.6 0.6 1" contype="0" conaffinity="0"/>
      <body name="tip_link" pos="0 0 -0.45">
        <inertial pos="0 0 0" mass="0.05" diaginertia="0.0001 0.0001 0.0001"/>
        <geom name="tip_a_contact_geom" type="sphere" size="0.03"
              rgba="0.8 0.2 0.2 1"/>
        <!-- reference_frame: "body" resolves through this one (identity). -->
        <site name="tip_a_ft_site" pos="0 0 0" size="0.003" group="3"/>
        <!-- reference_frame: "site" resolves through this one (rotated). -->
        <site name="tip_a_bracket" pos="0 0 0" quat="0.5 -0.5 -0.5 0.5"
              size="0.003" group="3"/>
      </body>
    </body>

    <body name="ground">
      <geom name="ground_box" type="box" size="2 2 0.05" pos="0 0 0"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>

  <actuator>
    <position name="m1" joint="j1" kp="50" kv="5" ctrlrange="-3.14 3.14"/>
  </actuator>

  <sensor>
    <contact name="tip_a_contact"
             geom1="tip_a_contact_geom"
             num="1"
             data="found force torque dist pos normal tangent"
             reduce="netforce"/>
  </sensor>
</mujoco>
